  "2026-11-07T15:13:23.163Z",codex-agent,"Final source certification: npm run release:check passed in 683 seconds and bun run release:check passed in 802 seconds, serially in about 25 minutes with at most two workers and isolated HOME/Git settings. Each passed 67 unskipped tests including 500 seeded journal sequences; 100 percent of 573 statements, 364 branches, 129 functions and 500 lines across nine runtime modules; one packed npm/Bun acceptance; 57 expected behavioral mutation failures; and 62 restored tests. Pinned-pm linked verification passed 31 tests. Exact Node 22.19.0 and 26.13.0 separately passed all 11 spawn-diagnostic/privacy tests each. Typecheck, lint, zero duplication, 97 documented declarations, native tracker health, identity/privacy, zero production audit vulnerabilities, 44-file pack allowlist, changelog and publication attestation pass at unchanged thresholds. Both accepted archives match SHA-256 a1ff2149e130d23cb9749d9e4b70ba1f5394cfd305757ffd53f5359ab8dc31c5, unchanged from the preceding runtime fix; each manager executes 56 primary CLI calls plus SDK/runtime probes with Git absent. The new development gates preserve all 2449 refused and 566 allowed spellings and frozen latency receipts. The preliminary 159-second full run was intentionally stopped for work-guard corrections and is retained above; both final full runs passed without a local timeout or advisory-endpoint retry. Four inherited histories retain main as an exact byte prefix; one changed history is branch-only. No new SDK gap, dependency-pin change, weakened regression or product semantics change. New-head hosted checks remain pending and separate evidence. No thread reply/resolution, merge or release."
  "2026-11-07T17:06:42.971Z",codex-agent,"Auto round 5: clean worktree and current remote head verified; main is included. Fetched all unresolved threads and every comment with no remaining pages; latest CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range section. All five findings are valid. Class rules: documented settings must match executable bounds; invariant selections and hashes must be computed once per journal/certificate query; lexical home detection must be stable across wrappers/delimiters and cover supported resolved/WSL aliases without filesystem access; recipe identity must bind transitive fixture implementations. Will add byte-stable allow/refuse corpora, real nongit SDK/CLI and packed consumer cases, deterministic hash-count regressions, and fixture-bound recipe tests. Frozen historical receipts and fixture bytes remain immutable."
