  "2026-11-07T18:04:38.319Z",codex-agent,"Final class-boundary audit caught an overmatch introduced during this round: extending every Windows mount and network share profile alternative to include root also rejected ordinary public root-named folders. Restricted root-home recognition to native Linux/WSL homes and the known physical root-home aliases; Windows mounts and generic network shares retain their original Users/home profile rule. Added six public-path controls and two distinguishing overmatch mutations, preserving every prior test. The corpus now has 3070 refused and 775 allowed spellings. The first npm release gate passed (72 tests, all counters covered, 73 distinguishing reverts and 71 restored tests), but its broader classifier is superseded; final npm and Bun gates will run against this corrected boundary."
  "2026-11-07T18:08:26.519Z",codex-agent,"Boundary refinement: Windows drive identity must survive colon tokenization before classifying the rooted component. The fixed classifier now retains it, so an ordinary drive-rooted public root directory is not mistaken for the Linux root home. Generic network root directories likewise remain public; physical root-home aliases are limited to known native forms. Added a classifier-only property covering those paths, with three mutations (Windows-profile broadening, network-share broadening, lost drive context) required to fail at proof:public_root_scope. The independent pinned SDK secret scanner intentionally remains stricter for the four drive-rooted controls; these classifier/identity controls do not change its policy or defer any acceptance criterion. All prior must-allow inputs are preserved. Final corpora: 3074 refused spellings, 773 SDK-admissible/public controls, plus four classifier-only drive controls. Pinned-pm focused verification passed all 42 tests; all 76 behavioral mutations (57 retained plus 19 new) and final npm/Bun gates follow on this frozen implementation."
