  "2026-11-08T01:51:59.806Z",pi-reduce1,"Round 6 (auto re-review) continuation by pi-reduce1: both non-blocking findings fixed and their classes closed.\n\nFinding PRRT_kwDOVlPkts606CG8 (src/schema.ts guardSubmitted string scanning). Rule violated: admission work per submitted input must be bounded by distinct caller-allocated content, never multiplied by reference count. guardSubmitted re-ran the control scan, containsPrivateHomePath and scanMutationSecrets for every reference to the same string, so one 8000-character string referenced 32,767 times scanned roughly 260 million characters before the schema rejected the input. Fix: strings that passed every check are cached per submission, a repeated reference costs one Set lookup, the 32,768-visit ceiling still bounds total references, and a string that fails any check is never cached. Class search: guardSubmitted is the package's single shared pre-write guard behind all six commands, the SDK and CLI paths, JSON and TOON input, packed npm/Bun consumers and non-git trackers (one implementation, one fix covers every path); the identity gate scans each distinct tracked file once, the proof corpus scans each distinct text once, kernel digest reuse was closed in the previous round, and output rendering is bounded by the 32 KiB envelope ceiling, so no other per-reference content scanner exists. Tests: \"privacy scans bound repeated string references by distinct content\" (property across 2/64/2048 repeated references with a deterministic regex-execution counter plus distinct-content scaling, proof:string_scan_budget), \"SDK admission bounds repeated string references before any owner mutation\" (4096 shared references refused pre-effect, no journal events, proof:string_scan_sdk), \"CLI repeated string references scan once, refuse inertly and accept valid repeats\" (JSON and TOON renderers stay inert, repeated private labels refused, valid shared labels accepted, proof:string_scan_cli). Revert proof: mutation \"repeated str