  "2026-11-08T09:18:35.901Z",claude-orchestrator,"Orchestrator fix for CodeRabbit thread PRRT_kwDOVlPkts60_ZcL (src/privacy.ts:12), after the PR reached 6 automatic rounds. Rule: sentence punctuation is not part of a path, so a home alias followed by one or more periods must classify like the bare alias. containsPrivateHomePath now trims trailing dots from each token with an index loop (linear on long dot runs), and '.' joins the bare-root delimiter set. All consumers (SDK schema guard, identity gate, corpus privacy) share this one classifier. Corpus (test/home-paths.ts): forbidden adds the root alias with '.', '...', '. ' and '.\\n', and the four bare aliases (var/home, var/root, private/var/root, System/Volumes/Data/Users) with '', '.', '...' and '. ' tails, also inside a sentence. Allowed controls: bare /home. and /Users., /root.ts, relative docs paths, /var/log., /public/fixture... and a run of 5,000 dots. Revert proof: with only src/privacy.ts reverted, 2 privacy tests fail (public corpus guard; mounted profile aliases); restored, 29/29 pass. Full unit suite 77/77; typecheck, lint and identity gate pass (the gate caught a literal alias in the first draft of this fix's code comment)."
